         'Every person\'s life has a particular purpose, and in achieving it his beliefs, reason, knowledge and social values guide him. In the same way, the collective national life of every nation has a defined purpose, for which its members struggle together in the light of a collective way of thinking. This collective thinking is called the ideology of that nation. For example, before the creation of Pakistan the national aim of the Muslims of South Asia was a Muslim state where they could live in freedom. The collective thought that guided them was that Muslims are a distinct nation separate from the Hindus and should therefore have a separate homeland of their own. This national aim, and the collective thinking behind achieving it, came to be called the Ideology of Pakistan.',
